---
// Course Details hero (Task 2, Course PDP Chunk A) — Figma 675:4353
// (desktop, ≥1024, file FX7PDNvhZwyozODaq8Q8i7) / 1109:14377 (mobile — the
// "Sole Switch Pro Page" > "Course Details" instance inside the
// professional-courses mobile frame 1109:14374). Same buybox-left /
// visual-right SHAPE as ../pdp/ProductDetails.astro (eyebrow, title,
// StarRating, price, CTA row, short copy) and reuses that section's exact
// eyebrow markup + StarRating import, but two real content differences —
// both intentional, not oversights:
//
// 1. The right column is a branded teal course card ("SoleSwitch / Pro
//    Course" + a "For Health Professionals" tag), not an image gallery.
//    Figma's own layer for this card is a single flattened raster image
//    (`imgRectangle41` in get_design_context's output) — no real text/fill
//    layers to read — the same situation PdpReviews.astro hit for its
//    screenshot-only "Reviews Plugin" frame. Per that precedent
//    ("reference build, not a raw asset dump"), the card is rebuilt here as
//    real markup + DS tokens (teal background, bold display title, yellow
//    tag), reading the visible pixels/text off the screenshot rather than
//    embedding a copy of the PNG. `titleLines` is an array (not a single
//    wrapped string) so the exact Figma line break ("SoleSwitch" / "Pro
//    Course" — identical on both desktop and mobile screenshots, so it's a
//    deliberate break, not width-dependent reflow) renders reliably instead
//    of depending on font-metric-sensitive text wrapping.
//
// 2. Figma's buy box literally reuses the PRODUCT hero's cart affordances —
//    a two-pill course-tier toggle ("Sole Switch Basic" outline / "Sole
//    Switch Pro" filled-selected) plus a quantity stepper + "Add to Cart"
//    button. Sole Switch Pro is fulfilled on Kajabi, not the Shopify cart,
//    so per this task's brief the purchase flow is remapped rather than
//    copied literally:
//    - The filled "Add to Cart" button becomes this hero's PRIMARY CTA, an
//      outbound "Enroll Now" link to `item.pdp.enrollHref`
//      (target="_blank", rel="noopener noreferrer") — no cart.js import, no
//      quantity stepper (Kajabi enrollment isn't a quantity purchase).
//    - The outline "Sole Switch Basic" pill becomes the SECONDARY CTA, kept
//      as a real link (its Figma label, verbatim) to the Basic-tier course
//      page (`/courses/sole-switch`, an existing placeholder route — see
//      sitemap.js).
//    - The filled "Sole Switch Pro" pill is dropped: it's the tier already
//      being viewed on this exact page, so keeping it as a 3rd
//      button-styled element would both be redundant with the primary
//      Enroll CTA and exceed the brief's explicit "two CTAs" instruction.
//    See coursepdp-task-2-report.md for the full reasoning + screenshots.
//
// `item.pdp.heroTitle` overrides the catalog's shorter `item.title` for
// just this <h1> (Figma reads "Sole Switch Pro Course", the catalog's
// `title` is "Sole Switch Pro" — used elsewhere for nav/breadcrumbs/PLP
// cards/page <title>, so it's left alone) — same targeted-override pattern
// as ProductDetails' `item.pdp.ctaLabel`. `item.rating`/`item.reviewCount`
// are sourced top-level exactly like ProductDetails does (mirrored per the
// task brief), not duplicated under `pdp`.
//
// No client script: every interactive element here is a plain <a> (real
// navigation), so there's nothing to init/leak. `data-pdp-id` is kept on
// the <section> for parity with ProductDetails/debugging only.
//
// ---- Component-generalization fixes (Chunk B1 Task 2 follow-up) ----------
// Sole Switch (Basic)'s Figma frame (998:14854/999:7197) genuinely diverges
// from the Sole Switch Pro frame this component was originally built
// against, in three ways now made data-driven instead of hardcoded:
//
// 1. Sale price. `item.pdp.compareAtPrice` is the same OPTIONAL field
//    ProductDetails.astro already uses (its guard idiom + class names
//    `-sale`/`-compare` are reused verbatim here) — when absent (Sole
//    Switch Pro), the price renders exactly as before (no wrapping <span>,
//    same single text node); when present (Sole Switch: "$50 USD"), a
//    struck-through compare-at price renders beside the sale price.
//
// 2. Course card colour. `item.pdp.courseCard.variant` is an OPTIONAL
//    string ('yellow' | unset). NavCard.astro takes an arbitrary `variant`
//    string and interpolates it directly (`nav-card--${variant}`); this
//    component doesn't reuse that interpolation — it just checks
//    `variant === 'yellow'` and toggles one fixed modifier class, since
//    'yellow' is the only variant this course card has ever needed. Unset
//    (Sole Switch Pro) keeps the base
//    `.course-details__card` teal background byte-for-byte; `'yellow'`
//    (Sole Switch) adds a `--yellow` modifier class. Figma's own flattened
//    card image confirms the title text stays WHITE on both the teal AND
//    yellow cards (get_design_context + a close crop of the yellow card's
//    raster asset both show white "SOLESWITCH COURSE" text), so no
//    additional text-colour variant is needed for the title. The tag pill
//    (used only on the teal/Health-Professionals card) is unaffected.
//
// 3. Course card tag. `item.pdp.courseCard.tag` was already read but
//    unconditionally rendered as an empty pill when absent — now guarded
//    with the same optional-field idiom the rest of this file/Testimonial's
//    `role` already use (`item.pdp.courseCard.tag && <span>...</span>`), so
//    Sole Switch's tag-less Figma card renders no pill artifact.
//
// ---- Hero image branch (Chunk B1 Task 3 follow-up: component gap fix) ----
// Combating Bunions' Figma hero (675:5542 desktop / 999:7156 mobile) has no
// branded card at all — its right column raster (`imgRectangle41` in
// get_design_context's pull, node `I675:5542;173:147` desktop /
// `I999:7156;181:674` mobile) is a plain product photo, no overlaid text, no
// colored background (see catalog.js's `combating-bunions` entry, flagged as
// a STOP-and-report component gap by the task that first authored that
// item's data). `item.pdp.heroImage` is a second, OPTIONAL field for this
// case, guarded with the exact same `item.pdp?.x &&` idiom `courseCard`
// already uses — `courseCard` and `heroImage` are mutually exclusive
// (an item sets at most one; neither renders anything when both are unset).
//
// Shape: a plain string path, e.g. `overview.image` in CourseOverview.astro
// — not an object, and not ProductDetails.astro's `gallery` array. The
// gallery shape exists to drive thumbnail-swap interaction across MULTIPLE
// images; this hero has exactly one static image with no interaction, the
// same shape CourseOverview's single `image` field already models. Alt text
// is likewise NOT carried in the data (neither CourseOverview's `image` nor
// ProductDetails' gallery thumbs carry alt in catalog data — alt is always a
// judgment call made at render time in the component). Per YourInstructors
// .astro's placeholder-photo precedent (`alt=""` because the placeholder is
// a generic shot, not a real likeness — a name-echoing alt would misrepresent
// it), this image is likewise `alt=""`: it's a stand-in PLP course photo
// (see catalog.js) reused as decorative art beside an `<h1>` that already
// names the course in text, not a real product photo with informational
// content of its own yet. Unlike CourseOverview's image (below-the-fold,
// `loading="lazy"`), this one is the hero's own right column — the same
// above-the-fold position as ProductDetails' main gallery image, which
// intentionally omits `loading="lazy"` (only its secondary thumbnails lazy-
// load) — so this omits it too, to not delay this page's LCP candidate.
//
// Layout: mobile is a literal Figma `h-[210px] w-full` box — identical to
// `.course-details__card`'s own mobile fixed height (same frame, same slot).
// Desktop's node is unconstrained (`flex-[1_0_0] ... self-stretch`, no
// aspect-ratio in the pulled code) — rather than measuring one course's
// content height off its frame the way `.course-details__card`'s desktop
// `aspect-ratio: 556 / 399` literal does (a value specific to Sole Switch
// Pro's own buybox height), this stretches to match the buybox's actual
// rendered height via `align-self: stretch` with no fixed height/ratio at
// all — a plain image has no internal content forcing its own minimum size,
// so it cleanly inherits the row's cross-axis size from its sibling exactly
// like Figma's own `self-stretch` expresses, and stays correct regardless of
// how tall any given course's buybox content happens to be. The crop itself
// (Figma's absolutely-positioned `h-[166.97%] top-[-33.48%]` image) is the
// same object-fit:cover-via-Figma-percentages idiom CourseOverview.astro's
// own header comment already documents — reproduced as a plain
// overflow:hidden + object-fit:cover box, not the literal percentages.
import StarRating from '../plp/StarRating.astro';

const { item } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="course-details" data-pdp-id={item.id}>
  <div class="course-details__inner">
    <p class="course-details__eyebrow"><span>Gait Happens</span></p>

    <div class="course-details__layout">
      <div class="course-details__buybox">
        <div class="course-details__heading">
          <h1 class="course-details__title">{item.pdp?.heroTitle ?? item.title}</h1>
          <div class="course-details__rating">
            <StarRating rating={item.rating ?? 0} count={item.reviewCount ?? 0} />
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="course-details__price">
          {item.pdp?.compareAtPrice ? (
            <>
              <span class="course-details__price-sale">{item.pdp?.priceExact ?? item.price}</span>
              <span class="course-details__price-compare">{item.pdp.compareAtPrice}</span>
            </>
          ) : (
            item.pdp?.priceExact ?? item.price
          )}
        </p>

        {item.pdp?.description && <p class="course-details__intro">{item.pdp.description}</p>}

        <div class="course-details__tier">
          <span class="course-details__tier-label">Select your course</span>
          {item.pdp?.secondaryCta && (
            <a class="course-details__pill" href={item.pdp.secondaryCta.href}>
              {item.pdp.secondaryCta.label}
            </a>
          )}
        </div>

        <a
          class="course-details__enroll"
          href={item.pdp?.enrollHref ?? '#'}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          {item.pdp?.enrollLabel ?? 'Enroll Now'}
        </a>

        {item.pdp?.instructorsByline && (
          <div class="course-details__instructors">
            <span class="course-details__avatars" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="course-details__avatar"></span>
              <span class="course-details__avatar"></span>
            </span>
            <p class="course-details__instructors-text">{item.pdp.instructorsByline}</p>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>

      {item.pdp?.courseCard && (
        <div class={`course-details__card${item.pdp.courseCard.variant === 'yellow' ? ' course-details__card--yellow' : ''}`}>
          <p class="course-details__card-title">
            {item.pdp.courseCard.titleLines.map((line) => <span>{line}</span>)}
          </p>
          {item.pdp.courseCard.tag && <span class="course-details__card-tag">{item.pdp.courseCard.tag}</span>}
        </div>
      )}

      {item.pdp?.heroImage && (
        <div class="course-details__hero-image">
          <img src={item.pdp.heroImage} alt="" />
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .course-details__inner {
    max-width: var(--container-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-7);
    padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* Same eyebrow markup/styling as ProductDetails.astro — Figma shows a
     plain caption ("GAIT HAPPENS"), not a navigational breadcrumb trail. */
  .course-details__eyebrow {
    font: var(--type-caption);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caption);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .course-details__eyebrow span { display: inline-block; }

  .course-details__layout {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  /* ---- Buy box ---------------------------------------------------- */

  .course-details__buybox {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    /* Figma's own buybox column gap (675:4353) is a uniform --space-5 (24px)
       between every child, unlike ProductDetails' --space-6 — kept
       frame-specific per the pulled design context. */
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .course-details__heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .course-details__title {
    font: var(--type-h3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .course-details__rating {
    display: flex;
  }

  .course-details__price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font: var(--type-h4);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  /* Optional sale/compare-at price — same fields/idiom as
     ProductDetails.astro's `.pdp-details__price-sale`/`-compare` (Figma
     `--feedback-error` #c62828, not yet a DS token; `--color-ink-70` for the
     struck-through original). Inert (no red, no strikethrough) whenever
     `item.pdp.compareAtPrice` is unset, e.g. Sole Switch Pro. */
  .course-details__price-sale {
    color: #c62828;
  }
  .course-details__price-compare {
    font: var(--type-body-large);
    color: var(--color-ink-70);
    text-decoration: line-through;
  }

  .course-details__intro {
    font: var(--type-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .course-details__tier {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .course-details__tier-label {
    font: var(--type-caption);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caption);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* Secondary CTA — outline pill, matches ProductDetails' unselected size
     pill exactly (border-teal / paper bg / teal text). */
  .course-details__pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: fit-content;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-teal);
    background: var(--color-paper);
    color: var(--color-teal);
    font: var(--type-cta);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  /* Primary CTA — Enroll (external, Kajabi). Same teal-filled styling as
     ProductDetails' Add to Cart button (this frame's colors match — teal,
     not yellow, confirmed via the pulled screenshot, not assumed). */
  .course-details__enroll {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--color-teal);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font: var(--type-button);
    padding: var(--space-4) 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  .course-details__pill:hover,
  .course-details__enroll:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .course-details__instructors {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  /* The avatar pair stays a side-by-side row at both widths (6px apart per
     Figma); only the OUTER container flips to column on desktop so the pair
     sits above the byline. */
  .course-details__avatars {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  /* Flat placeholder circles — no real instructor photography yet; Task 7
     ("Your Instructors") owns real bios/photos further down the page. Fill
     reuses --color-border, the same "no photography yet" placeholder token
     ProductDetails' gallery media background already uses. */
  .course-details__avatar {
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-border);
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }
  .course-details__instructors-text {
    font: var(--type-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* ---- Branded course card (right column) ---------------------------- */

  .course-details__card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    /* --space-5 (not --space-7) on mobile: the card is a literal fixed
       210px-tall block there (Figma 1109:14377;181:674), and the 2-line
       --type-display title + tag pill need ~137px — --space-7 (48px, 96px
       total) would leave only 114px and risk overflowing that fixed height.
       Desktop has far more room (see aspect-ratio below) so it switches to
       the frame's literal --space-7 padding. */
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--color-teal);
    height: 210px;
  }
  /* Optional colour variant — unlike NavCard.astro's `nav-card--${variant}`
     interpolation (which accepts any variant string), this component only
     ever toggles a single fixed 'yellow' modifier class (see the header
     comment). Sole Switch's card (998:14856) is yellow with
     no tag; Sole Switch Pro's stays the base teal (no `variant` set) +
     its "For Health Professionals" tag. Figma's own flattened card raster
     confirms the title text stays white on both colours, so only the
     background changes here. */
  .course-details__card--yellow {
    background: var(--color-yellow);
  }
  .course-details__card-title {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    font: var(--type-display);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }
  .course-details__card-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    width: fit-content;
    background: var(--color-yellow);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font: var(--type-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caption);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  }

  /* ---- Hero image (right column) — mutually exclusive with the branded
     card above (see header comment). Mobile is a literal Figma-measured
     fixed 210px height, identical to `.course-details__card`'s own mobile
     height (999:7156;181:674 is the same slot/frame as the card's). */
  .course-details__hero-image {
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-border);
    height: 210px;
  }
  .course-details__hero-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .course-details__pill:hover,
    .course-details__enroll:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  /* ---- Desktop (Figma 675:4353, ≥1024) ------------------------------- */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .course-details__layout {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
    .course-details__buybox {
      flex: 0 0 484px;
      max-width: 484px;
    }
    /* Desktop (675:4353) stacks the avatar pair ABOVE the "Course By:"
       byline text; the base row layout is the mobile (1109:14377)
       arrangement. */
    .course-details__instructors {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    /* Only the enroll CTA needs the override — the outline pill is already
       width: fit-content in its base rule. */
    .course-details__enroll {
      width: fit-content;
    }
    .course-details__card {
      flex: 1 0 0;
      align-self: stretch;
      /* Card geometry measured off the 675:4353 frame itself: 1200 canvas −
         2×48 padding − 484 buybox − 64 gap = 556 wide; content-row height
         ≈399 (531 frame − 2×48 padding − eyebrow row). Fixed aspect-ratio
         (not the mobile fixed height) keeps the card proportional as the
         real container grows past Figma's 1200 canvas up to --container-max
         (1440) — same flexible-width/fixed-ratio approach ProductDetails'
         gallery media uses. */
      height: auto;
      aspect-ratio: 556 / 399;
      /* Desktop has ample height (≥399px) for the frame's own --space-7
         (48px) padding — mobile's smaller --space-5 above is a fixed-height
         fit constraint, not a desktop concern. */
      padding: var(--space-7);
    }
    /* Desktop hero image (675:5542;173:147) is unconstrained in Figma — no
       fixed height/aspect-ratio, just `self-stretch` — so unlike the card
       above this intentionally carries no aspect-ratio literal, letting it
       stretch to match the buybox's actual rendered height directly (see
       header comment). */
    .course-details__hero-image {
      flex: 1 0 0;
      align-self: stretch;
      height: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
